  "id": "perceptual-organization",
  "term": "perceptual organization",
  "definition": "Perceptual organization is the mental process of detecting and assembling visual elements into a meaningful whole, such as picking out a shape or contour from a surrounding background or noise. In this context, it is studied as the ability to extract forms from visual scenes using both fragmented and continuous closed-contour stimuli.",
